      "next_deadline": "No local capital NOFA; the CoC states it will provide letters of support and may allocate future HHAP to new interim or affordable units. HHAP-7 allocations are preliminary for FY 2026-27.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "Mendocino County has no housing department: the Executive Office Grants Division administers state CDBG and HOME program income, Social Services is the administrative entity for the Mendocino County Homeless Services Continuum of Care (CA-509) and HHAP, Behavioral Health and Recovery Services holds BHSA, NPLH and bridge housing, Planning and Building Services handles density bonus and the Housing Element, and the Community Development Commission of Mendocino County (CDC, the housing authority) supplies vouchers and owns housing. The County repealed its inclusionary ordinance on September 10, 2024, has no housing trust fund money, no NOFA and no impact fee waiver; County capital help has come from state pass-through grants (CDBG-DR, Homekey) and small HOME program income balances. Ukiah and Fort Bragg run their own programs (Pass 3). mendocinocounty.gov, the Legistar web API client 'mendocino', mendocino.granicusideas.com and cdchousing.org all open normally. HHAP is fully absorbed by shelter operations; its relevance to a developer is a CoC letter of support and possible operating subsidy for PSH units referred through Coordinated Entry. Source is the April 7, 2026 Board item on Granicus Ideas with the HHAP-6 regional application attached.",
